--- begin ---
PRE-REGISTRATION: per-layer activation tail, traced control against traced NOP copy, YOLOv8s. Desktop 2
(DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), 2026-10-15. Written before any NOP dispatch with the tail fields. Disclosed: one traced CONTROL
run with the new fields was made as a smoke (ctl a_tail sum 3,693,428 cycles); no NOP data with them exists.

Question. Per layer, how long after the layer's last activation task completes does the layer end (next marker), and
how much of that is compute? That sizes lever 1 of the overlap scope: hiding each layer's exposed compute tail behind
the next layer's transport (weight prefetch across the barrier, or relaxing the barrier where the next layer does not
read this one's output). The NOP sitting's fit put it at ~36,647 cycles per layer (~1.34 ms, DERIVED).

Instrument. tools/engine_shim_trace.py now records per layer, from the FINISHED_TASK pulses (exact: 1,387 of 1,387
activation and 99 of 99 weight completions on every layer in all 6 control runs of 20261015T1927Z):
a_done_first / a_done_last (offsets from the marker), a_tail = next marker - last activation completion, and the
same for weights. Nothing else in the tool changed; containers unchanged (build/yolov8s_tr_ctl.ignite and
build/yolov8s_tr_ctl_nop.ignite, hashed below).

Method. scratch/b45/sit_nop.py --rounds 6 (ctl and nop alternated, one cold traced dispatch per process), under
research-lowlevel.sh --npu, void unless timing_eligible true. Then scratch/b46/tail_verdict.py.

Gates: C, NOP/ctl frame 0.70-0.82. S, ctl frame within 2% of the NOP sitting's 27,935,540 cycles.
Rule T: X = sum over layers of (ctl a_tail - nop a_tail), mean of runs. X >= 1,800,000 cycles (1.0 ms DERIVED): GO
(prototype cross-layer overlap); 900,000-1,800,000: MARGINAL; < 900,000: NO (lever 2 probe next, lever 3 main line).
Expected: GO or MARGINAL (the fit's 1.34 ms is 2.4 M cycles, but it came from a residual model, not a direct timing).
Named limits: X is the opportunity, not a reachable saving. The next layer usually reads this layer's output, so how
much of the tail its transport can cover depends on which rows its first packets need; weights can be fetched early
regardless. ctl tail - nop tail also contains any drain slowed by late outputs, which is compute-caused all the same.
Reported, not verdict-bearing: per group, the head (marker to first activation completion), weight tails.

A hang, refused trace or contention voids the sitting.
--- end ---
verdict script, verbatim:
--- begin ---
"""Scratch: the pre-registered tail verdict. python -I tail_verdict.py <ctl trace json> <nop trace json>
Per layer, mean over runs of a_tail (next marker - last activation task completion), a_done_first, w_tail. Groups are
fixed from the committed control budget's warm compute share."""
import json
import sys
from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
ref = json.loads((ROOT / "results/aie/shim_trace_budget_yolov8s_desktop2_20261015T1922Z.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
cs = np.array([r["compute_share"] for r in ref["layers"]])
G = {"lo (<10%)": cs < 0.10, "mid (10-35%)": (cs >= 0.10) & (cs < 0.35), "hi (>=35%)": cs >= 0.35}
GHZ = 1.80


def load(p):
    d = json.loads(Path(p).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    if d["layers"] != [r["name"] for r in ref["layers"]]:
        raise SystemExit(f"{p}: layer list differs")
    runs = [r["shims"][sorted(r["shims"])[0]]["layers"] for r in d["runs"]]
    out = {}
    for key in ("cycles", "a_tail", "a_done_first", "w_tail"):
        vals = [[L[key] for L in run] for run in runs]
        if any(v is None for run in vals for v in run):
            raise SystemExit(f"{p}: {key} missing on some layer")
        out[key] = np.mean(np.array(vals, dtype=float), axis=0)
    return out, len(runs)


c, nc = load(sys.argv[1])
n, nn = load(sys.argv[2])
print(f"runs: ctl {nc}, nop {nn}")
print(f"{'group':14} {'n':>3} {'ctl tail':>10} {'nop tail':>10} {'d tail':>10} {'d ms':>7} {'ctl head':>10} {'nop head':>10}")
for g, m in G.items():
    dt = (c["a_tail"] - n["a_tail"])[m].sum()
    print(f"{g:14} {m.sum():3d} {c['a_tail'][m].sum():10,.0f} {n['a_tail'][m].sum():10,.0f} {dt:10,.0f} "
          f"{dt / GHZ / 1e6:7.3f} {c['a_done_first'][m].sum():10,.0f} {n['a_done_first'][m].sum():10,.0f}")
X = (c["a_tail"] - n["a_tail"]).sum()
print(f"\nframe: ctl window {c['cycles'].sum():,.0f}, nop window {n['cycles'].sum():,.0f}; ctl a_tail {c['a_tail'].sum():,.0f} "
      f"({c['a_tail'].sum() / c['cycles'].sum():.1%} of the window), nop a_tail {n['a_tail'].sum():,.0f}")
print(f"X = sum(ctl a_tail - nop a_tail) = {X:,.0f} cycles = {X / GHZ / 1e6:.3f} ms (DERIVED at {GHZ} GHz)")
print(f"w_tail: ctl {c['w_tail'].sum():,.0f}, nop {n['w_tail'].sum():,.0f}")
print("\n== rules (pre-registered) ==")
ratio = n["cycles"].sum() / c["cycles"].sum()
okc = 0.70 <= ratio <= 0.82
oks = abs(c["cycles"].sum() / 27_935_540 - 1) <= 0.02
print(f"C: nop/ctl frame {ratio:.3f} (0.70-0.82) -> {'PASS' if okc else 'FAIL'}")
print(f"S: ctl frame {c['cycles'].sum():,.0f} within 2% of the NOP sitting's 27,935,540 -> {'PASS' if oks else 'FAIL'}")
if not (okc and oks):
    print("C or S failed: T is not read")
verdict = "GO" if X >= 1_800_000 else "MARGINAL" if X >= 900_000 else "NO"
print(f"T: X {X:,.0f} cycles (>= 1,800,000 GO; 900,000-1,800,000 MARGINAL; < 900,000 NO) -> {verdict}")
--- end ---

